        "loading"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "a11y": {
    "role": "button (implicit from the <button> element)",
    "name": "`aria-label` required (or aria-labelledby). There is no visible text.",
    "keyboard": [
      "Enter — activates",
      "Space — activates on release"
    ],
    "focusIndicator": "Double ring: 4px outer with colors.accent.accent-alpha.8 and 2px inner with colors.accent.accent.3 (focus-ring layer in Figma).",
    "minTarget": "24px at size 1 (WCAG 2.5.8 minimum, no margin); size 2 / 3 / 4 = 32 / 40 / 48. Inside a size 2 TextField the button is 24px.",
    "contrastNote": "Icon against background ≥ 3:1 (WCAG 1.4.11, UI components), except disabled. Not measured in Figma: to be verified per variant.",
    "wcag": [
      "1.4.11 Non-text Contrast (AA)",
      "2.1.1 Keyboard",
      "2.4.7 Focus Visible",
      "2.5.8 Target Size (Minimum)",
      "4.1.2 Name, Role, Value"
    ]
  },
  "content": {
    "label": null,
    "note": "No visible text. The accessible name is aria-label: verb + object, without the word \"button\"."
  },
  "behavior": {
    "loading": {
      "indicator": "spinner",
      "replaces": "icon",
      "blocksInteraction": true,
      "keepsWidth": true
    },
    "overflow": "none",
    "motion": [
      {
        "on": "hover",
        "property": "background-color",
        "reducedMotion": "instant"
      }
    ],
    "responsive": []
  },
  "testing": {
    "cases": [
      "without aria-label the component warns in development (or does not compile in TypeScript)",
      "disabled and loading do not emit onPress",
      "loading adds aria-busy, shows the spinner and keeps the size",
      "the icon uses the size from layout.iconSize according to size",
      "highContrast uses step 12 in all variants and colors",
      "each variant × color × state uses the tokens from tokens.bindings",
      "type defaults to 'button'"
    ]
  },
  "anchors": {
    "figma": {
      "file": "https://www.figma.com/design/pTGbM1i9PKc6858ef7498a/Radix-Themes--Community-",
      "node": "889:141070"
    },
    "code": {
      "importPath": "@/components/icon-button/icon-button",
      "export": "IconButton"
    }
  },
  "meta": {
    "source": "figma",
    "derivableFromSource": [
      "props.default",
      "layout",
      "tokens.bindings"
    ],
    "needsReview": [
      "Figma marks default values with ✦ (\"solid ✦\", \"2 ✦\", \"default ✦\"): the real value goes unmarked in the contract.",
      "The Figma axis is \"highContrast\" here (in Button it is \"highConstrast\", a typo). Checked: in IconButton it is spelled correctly.",
      "Background, border, shadow and opacity tokens read from the content-container layer at size 2 for the 6 variants × accent / neutral and, for error, solid and outline. Assumed to hold for the other sizes, and for error in classic / soft / surface / ghost (same pattern as Button).",
      "The icon color (iconColor) could NOT be read in most variants: the icon is an instance and its fills are not accessible. Only solid + accent + default was confirmed (tokens.colors.accent-contrast). The rest was copied from Button (text): a reasonable assumption, verify by hand.",
      "The icon color in disabled (neutral-alpha.8) and in highContrast are also assumptions copied from Button.",
      "The radius is bound and was verified at all 4 sizes: radius.1-max to radius.4-max.",
      "Widths and heights (24 / 32 / 40 / 48) and icon size (16 / 16 / 18 / 20) are loose in Figma, with no variable. The tokens tokens.space.button-height-N are used because the values match Button.",
      "loading=true only exists in Figma together with state=disable. The spinner is 16px at size 2; the other sizes were not verified.",
      "opacity on hover / active (0.88, 0.82, 0.92) is fixed in Figma, with no variable, same as in Button.",
      "classic uses two gradient layers (white → transparent) with no variable. They are not in tokens.",
      "The focus ring was copied from Button (accent); it was not read in IconButton.",
      "Contrast and touch area not measured. At 24px in size 1, 2.5.8 is met right at the limit.",
      "Not in Figma: aria-label, type, onPress."
    ]
  }
}
